# interplay_versions_suspend_info_2_245: The blob's device info is written at the version the device has when it suspends, up to the last query's max key (DeviceCore::serialize_suspend_state; device_info::write_device_info reads the device's current features): a guest that queried at 245 and lowered to 43 migrates a 43 blob (no keys 17, 19, 21, 23-27, 36; key 28 without bit 1), and one that queried at 2 and raised to 245 a 245 blob. Each resumes onto a fresh device, whose capability check runs at the blob's version and passes; the resumed guest queries again, and a second migration carries the max key the first blob named.
